    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Seiya Suzuki** (74.67) and **James Wood** (72.12) anchor our offensive production. **Suzuki** benefits from an elite combination of a favorable hitter\u2019s park and a soft matchup against Sugano, while **Wood** leverages his xwOBA profile and the leadoff spot to maximize run-scoring potential against Houser. We are also high on **Max Muncy** (69.13), who avoids the typical platoon tax against Gasser and benefits from a high-upside matchup against a sub-5.00 xERA starter. While **Josh Naylor** (66.29) faces a tough platoon disadvantage and historical BvP hurdles, the venue-specific park factors keep him firmly in the \"Strong\" start category.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today was benching **Cole Young** (51.82). Despite his ability to exploit the opposing battery's slow delivery to boost his stolen base outlook\u2014a crucial asset in our pursuit of the SB category\u2014he fell just short of the efficiency threshold when compared to the ceiling of **Kyle Karros** (51.87). **Karros** secured the start primarily due to the venue\u2019s favorable park dynamics, which outweighed the marginal gains we would have seen from **Young** on the basepaths. Elsewhere, we are exercising caution with **Gabriel Moreno** and **Vinnie Pasquantino**; both remain in the starting lineup but face high-caliber arms in Meyer and Eovaldi, respectively, requiring us to monitor their real-time engagement closely to preserve our weekly game caps.",
